Attribution for the LIT golden-parity fixtures in this directory
=================================================================

torch_interface.npz holds numbers (weights, inputs and outputs at tiny dimensions) produced by running the PyTorch
interface classes of the MolmoAct2 LIT fork, which is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  _GoalSE3Encoder, _GoalPoseDecoder, _SemanticVisualCrossAttentionBlock, _SemanticVisualSelfAttentionBlock,
  _SemanticVisualAggregatorGroup, _SemanticVisualAggregator
  from src/lerobot/policies/molmoact2/modeling_molmoact2.py
  of https://github.com/jianmanlincjx/lerobot at commit b34a9200c1fc8a6986986ec9252a1197881fabeb
  (the lerobot submodule of https://github.com/jianmanlincjx/Molmoact2, Apache-2.0; lerobot itself is
  Copyright 2024 The HuggingFace Inc. team, Apache-2.0).
  sha256 of the file used: 353172664570e485e59065cd0bf60500dc6312b35c601b9fdd9ab792415c6f65 (also stored in the npz as
  meta/source_sha256).

The method is from "Breaking the Vision-Action Shortcut: Latent Interface Training for Generalizable Robot Foundation
Models", code at https://github.com/MAGICLAB-NUS/LIT (Apache-2.0).

gen_torch_fixture.py does not contain or copy that source: it extracts the classes from a local checkout of the file by AST
at run time. src/openpi/models/lit.py is an independent JAX implementation of the same computation, written from the
class behaviour and the parameter shapes of the released checkpoints.

torch_pi05_header_shapes.npz holds only tensor names and shapes read from the safetensors headers of the released
checkpoints https://huggingface.co/linjianman/LIT (pi05/lit_stage1, pi05/lit_stage2), for an informational comparison.
The pi0.5 plugin (https://github.com/jianmanlincjx/Pi05) carries no licence: it was read as a behavioural reference
only and none of its code is used here.

